cat > /tmp/codex-pr-334-review.md <<'"'MD'
# PR #334 Review

## Findings

### MUST-FIX
1. Contradictory trait guidance in the same skill doc: this PR now states that plan documents must use full trait slugs ("'`trait-*`), but the earlier Plan Document Format example still uses a short trait name (`error-guidance`). This will mislead users who follow the primary example.

### SHOULD-FIX
1. `.claude/skills/spec-plan/SKILL.md:191` says that YAML scalar values containing double quotes cause parse failures. That is too broad. Double quotes inside plain scalar text can be valid; the shown failure is specifically malformed mixed quoting (`"kspec foo" is run`).

### SUGGESTION
1. `.claude/skills/spec-plan/SKILL.md:152` combines broken and corrected trait examples in one YAML block, which introduces duplicate keys (`traits`). Consider separate blocks (or `---` separators) for cleaner copy/paste behavior.

